Vālin begs Sugrīva not to blame him citing fate-delusion --- Vālin grants kingdom and accepts Yama journey --- Vālin entrusts dearer-than-life Aṅgada to Sugrīva --- Vālin praises wise Tārā demanding obedience --- Vālin urges serving Rāma and surrenders golden garland --- Sugrīva grief-stricken accepts garland --- Vālin counsels Aṅgada obeying Sugrīva avoiding extremes --- Vālin dies baring teeth --- Monkeys despair as Tārā clasps Vālin like creeper
